    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction prioritizes high-upside speed and favorable matchups against sub-par starters. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Trea Turner** (79.76) anchor our offensive strategy; both benefit from the highly exploitable Andrew Abbott and Shane Baz, respectively. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, bolstered by a 16% park factor and the specific advantage of a slow opposing delivery that creates a high probability for stolen base volume. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (78.40) is locked into a strong platoon advantage against the struggling Andrew Abbott, making him a critical piece for accumulating power production. While **Yordan Alvarez** (52.37) boasts an elite xwOBA of 0.479, his score is depressed by a difficult platoon matchup against the left-handed Alvarez, illustrating our commitment to efficiency over raw talent in this specific rotation.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved keeping **Nelson Velazquez** (55.26) on the bench. Despite a stellar 0.418 xwOBA, his efficiency score fell just short of **Carson Benge** (55.45), whose slightly more favorable park factors and higher slot in the order pushed him over the threshold. We are keeping a close watch on **Gary Sanchez** (40.18), whose low score reflects a difficult matchup against Dobbins and negative park adjustments; he remains in the lineup only due to positional scarcity. Conversely, **Caleb Durbin** (62.58) continues to provide excellent value against the weak 5.07 xERA of Schultz, offering a reliable floor as we navigate a day where we must balance our daily game caps against maximizing our stolen base potential.",
